From: Sherif Shalaby <sherif2222222@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:21:31 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] gd: hal: give the HIDL HAL lookup 5s before aborting

On msm8930, hwservicemanager spends ~1s trying to lazy-start the absent
IBluetoothHci 1.1 before returning, so the 500ms watchdog killed
com.android.bluetooth even though the 1.0 HAL was registered.
---
 system/gd/hal/hci_hal_android_hidl.cc | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/system/gd/hal/hci_hal_android_hidl.cc b/system/gd/hal/hci_hal_android_hidl.cc
index 84e72d0..7b78bc3 100644
--- a/system/gd/hal/hci_hal_android_hidl.cc
+++ b/system/gd/hal/hci_hal_android_hidl.cc
@@ -434,7 +434,7 @@ class HciHalHidl : public HciHal {
           }
           LOG_ALWAYS_FATAL("Unable to get a Bluetooth service after 500ms, start the HAL before starting Bluetooth");
         }),
-        std::chrono::milliseconds(500));
+        std::chrono::milliseconds(5000));  // slow devices: hwservicemanager alone takes ~1s to report a missing 1.1 HAL
 
     bt_hci_1_1_ = IBluetoothHci_1_1::tryGetService();  // don't block on a 1.1 HAL that does not exist
 
